    "Task 4.8 – Diabetes Reflection \n",
    "1. What is an outlier? An outlier is a value noticeably different from most other values in a dataset.\n",
    "2. Three possible causes: An unusual value may come from a data-entry error, a measurement problem, or a genuine but rare patient measurement.\n",
    "3. Which variables showed the clearest visual outliers? Examine your box plots for age, BMI, HbA1c, and blood glucose, then identify the variables that visibly have points far outside their whiskers. Add your observation after running Task 4.2.\n",
