    "5. How many did IQR flag? Enter the BMI count printed by Task 4.5. The rule used was values outside Q1 − 1.5 × IQR and Q3 + 1.5 × IQR.\n",
    "6. Why can Z-Score and IQR disagree? Z-Score measures distance from the mean using standard deviation; IQR uses quartiles and is generally less affected by extreme observations.\n",
    "7. When should an outlier be retained? Retain a value if it is plausible and there is no evidence it is an error, especially in medical data where unusual patients are important.\n",
    "8. When might removal be justified? After confirming the value is a recording or measurement error, or when a documented analysis scope excludes it for a defensible reason.\n",
    "9. What happened to descriptive statistics? Use the before-and-after table from Task 4.7. Explain the observed change in mean, median, and standard deviation, rather than guessing.\n",
    "10. How could untreated outliers affect ML? They may distort scaling, averages, regression coefficients, or distance calculations; some real rare cases may also be valuable predictive information.\n",
